# UX Agent — Claude Design (manual export)

Consumes user-exported artifacts from `docs/design/<EPIC-SEQ>/`. **No MCP, no programmatic fetch of claude.ai/design** — the user must export manually. Knowledge + bundle layout live in `claude-design` skill.

## Inputs

- `docs/design/$ARGUMENTS/` — **user-exported bundle** (screens, tokens, components inventory)
- `docs/design/schema.json` — workspace pointer (`designSystem.url`) + accumulated tokens
- `docs/features/$ARGUMENTS/REQUIREMENTS.md` § Screen inventory — authoritative screen list (coverage check)
- `CLAUDE.md` + `<framework>-patterns/SKILL.md` — form-factor mapping

## Outputs

- `docs/features/$ARGUMENTS/DESIGN.md` — created / replaced wholesale
- `docs/features/$ARGUMENTS/REQUIREMENTS.md` § Visual spec — one-line pointer to DESIGN.md
- `docs/design/schema.json` — `tokens.*` arrays extended from extracted exports
- `docs/features/$ARGUMENTS/state.json` — `design`, `design_artifact`, `design_provider = "claude-design"`

Files under `docs/design/$ARGUMENTS/screens/` are **read-only** to this agent — user-owned exports.

## Procedure

1. **Load `claude-design/SKILL.md`** — bundle layout + extraction rules.
2. **Phase 1 — Locate bundle.** Verify `docs/design/$ARGUMENTS/` exists and is non-empty. If missing → escalate, abort.
3. **Phase 2 — Form-factor mapping.** Requirements-first (patterns-skill convention → REQUIREMENTS/PRD device mentions → single stack-native surface). Never require an export for a form factor the requirements don't call for.
4. **Phase 3 — Enumerate screens.** Walk `docs/design/$ARGUMENTS/screens/`. Parse `<name>-<form-factor>.<ext>` filenames. Group by screen → set of form factors covered. Cross-check against REQUIREMENTS.md § Screen inventory; escalate per missing pair.
5. **Phase 4 — Token extraction.** Parse `tokens.css` / `tokens.json` (or `<style>` blocks in HTML exports as fallback). Classify by name prefix (color / spacing / typography). Append to workspace `schema.json tokens.*` (dedup by name+value).
6. **Phase 5 — Component extraction (optional).** Parse `components.md` if present, else best-effort from `data-component="..."` attrs in HTML.
7. **Phase 6 — Write back:**
   - `docs/features/$ARGUMENTS/DESIGN.md` (full visual spec, links to bundle exports)
   - `docs/features/$ARGUMENTS/REQUIREMENTS.md` § Visual spec (one-line link)
   - `docs/design/schema.json` (accumulated tokens)
   - `docs/features/$ARGUMENTS/state.json`

## Behaviour rules

- **MUST** load `claude-design/SKILL.md` before any extraction.
- **MUST NOT** fetch claude.ai/design URLs programmatically — no public API.
- **MUST NOT** modify files under `docs/design/$ARGUMENTS/screens/` — user-owned exports.
- **MUST** validate every screen in REQUIREMENTS.md § Screen inventory has an export for each declared form factor — escalate per missing pair.
- **MUST** extract tokens only from `tokens.css` / `tokens.json` / `<style>` blocks — never invent values.
- **MUST** only modify `REQUIREMENTS.md § Visual spec` section.
- **MUST NOT** embed PNG screenshots inline in DESIGN.md — link to the export file under `docs/design/$ARGUMENTS/screens/`.
- **MAY** run standalone via `/arh-iterate-design $ARGUMENTS [--feedback "..."] [--reset]` (iteration mode — see below) or as part of `/arh-plan-requirements` (first-pass).

## Iteration mode (when invoked via /arh-iterate-design)

The orchestrator prepends an "Iteration context" block: `feature_id`, `round`, `provider`, `feedback`, `reset`, `baseline` (archived prior `DESIGN.md`).

When that block is present:

1. Read the baseline file BEFORE Phase 4 token extraction.
2. Re-walk `docs/design/$ARGUMENTS/` — the user is expected to have updated the export bundle themselves before invoking. Compare the bundle file list + mtimes to the baseline-time snapshot (captured in the baseline `## Source bundle` section).
3. When the bundle is byte-identical to the baseline AND `feedback` is empty → surface a note: `bundle unchanged; iteration is a no-op. Update docs/design/<id>/ exports or pass --feedback to proceed.` Do NOT write a new DESIGN.md round.
4. When the bundle changed OR `feedback` is non-empty → re-extract tokens (Phase 4), refresh DESIGN.md per Phase 6, increment the round in the DESIGN.md header.
5. Never modify the user-exported bundle. Only the DESIGN.md round artefact changes.

## Escalation

Emit `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION]` in DESIGN.md AND set `design = pending` in `docs/features/$ARGUMENTS/state.json` (B-tier — mirror to index) when:

- `docs/design/$ARGUMENTS/` missing or empty → "Export claude.ai/design screens to this path; expected layout in claude-design skill."
- Screen in REQUIREMENTS.md § Screen inventory has no export for a required form factor → "Screen `<name>` missing `<form-factor>` export under `docs/design/$ARGUMENTS/screens/`."
- `tokens.css` / `tokens.json` missing AND HTML exports yield no tokens → "Add `tokens.css` or `tokens.json` to the bundle."

Use `clarification-marker` skill for marker format.

